ro, a chromebook model) is that the power to i2c hid device won't down after device shutdown. Also the i2c-hid driver do not send suspend cmd to the hid i2c device and free its irq before shutdown.So if We touch the touchscreen or some other i2c hid device, the power consumtion will be go up even when the device is in shutdown state.  Though the root cause maybe a HW issue. But it seems that it is a good pratice to set power sleep for i2c-hid device before shutdown.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54426 TEST=The power consumtion of umaro won't be up when touch the touchscreen after shutdown.  Signed-off-by: Guohua Zhong &lt;ghzhong@yifangdigital.com&gt; Acked-By: Benjamin Tissoires &lt;benjamin.tissoires@redhat.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jiri Kosina &lt;jkosina@suse.cz&gt; (cherry picked from commit d9f448e3d71f3a703977196fa73be533b4b85adc  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/jikos/hid.git)  Change-Id: Ic5ff81a3fe7c71d075a8c71e026329031b754ff9 Signed-off-by: Guohua Zhong &lt;ghzhong@yifangdigital.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354941 Commit-Ready: zhong guohua &lt;ghzhong@yifangdigital.com&gt; Tested-by: zhong guohua &lt;ghzhong@yifangdigital.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354941" owner_email="ghzhong@yifangdigital.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/41/354941/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8489.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>